        "content": "<p>I tried using <code>try?</code> on a goal like this, but it threw the error that <code>simp</code> throws:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c\">/-</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">  Tactic `simp` failed with a nested error:</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">  maximum recursion depth has been reached</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">  use `set_option maxRecDepth &lt;num&gt;` to increase limit</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">  use `set_option diagnostics true` to get diagnostic information</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">  -/</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">try?</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Ideally <code>try?</code> would catch this error and still tell me that <code>grind</code> works.</p>",
        "id": 573384498,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1770843078
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I guess more precisely this is the error that <code>simp [*]</code> throws.</p>",
        "id": 573396656,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1770847862
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Note that it is correct behavior to not silence resource errors like this</p>",
        "id": 573683026,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1770969275
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(otherwise the tactic behavior would be a function of resources consumed so far, which is very fragile)</p>",
        "id": 573683160,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1770969341
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I suppose <code>try?</code> is a weird case since unlike other tactics it is not meant to be left in any persistent code, unlike <code>aesop</code> which has to be more principled in not silencing these.</p>",
        "id": 573683309,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1770969411
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I run into this sometimes when i accidentally add a hypothesis that allows simp to loop. It's a bit frustrating</p>",
        "id": 579279034,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Roos",
        "timestamp": 1773411418
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/issues/13216\">https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/issues/13216</a></p>",
        "id": 582814512,
        "sender_full_name": "Moritz Roos",
        "timestamp": 1774966764
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"310045\">Eric Wieser</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/270676-lean4/topic/.60try.3F.60.20fails.20if.20.60simp.60.20fails/near/573683309\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I suppose <code>try?</code> is a weird case since unlike other tactics it is not meant to be left in any persistent code, unlike <code>aesop</code> which has to be more principled in not silencing these.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>IMO interactive tactics (like <code>try?</code>/<code>rw??</code> etc) from the user perspective are more like a feature of lsp/ide. The fact that it is a tactic under the hood is only an implementation detail, we shouldn't think of it as a tactic.</p>",
        "id": 582861111,
        "sender_full_name": "Jakub Nowak",
